# Formatting-only commits that `git blame` (and GitHub's blame view) should skip.
#
# One commit hash per line. Full 40-char hashes, no indentation. Comments and
# blank lines are ignored. Newest entries go at the bottom.
#
# Why: a repo-wide reformat touches hundreds of lines that nobody reviewed for
# their content. Listing the commit here keeps `git blame` pointing at the last
# commit that actually changed each line.
#
# Local setup — once per clone (git does not read this file automatically):
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub applies this file automatically on the default branch, provided the
# commits listed here exist there. If the formatting commit is squash-merged or
# rebased, its hash changes — update the entry (or land it with a merge commit).

